<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2004"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 4:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kanas.com article: <BR>Posted on Thu, Dec. 16, 2004 <BR> <BR>Title: Residents fearful after park search <BR> <BR>&#34;One unsolved murder that has drawn attention since BTK resurfaced is the 1996 killing of 20-year-old Avanthea Williams. Her body was found Oct. 30 of that year in an apartment building just a block north of Murdock Park. <BR> <BR> <BR>Word of the package found in the park was unsettling to some of the people who work across the street.&#34; <BR> <BR>Could BTK be send a message by leaving it in this park?  Who was charged with the Avanthea muder?   <BR> <BR>Note that Avanthea&#39;s last name is the same as the of Anna Williams.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2004-->
<!--Post: 2009--><!--Time: 1103244216-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2009"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 4:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I see that the Avanthea murder is a cold case as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2009-->
<!--Post: 2295--><!--Time: 1103501790-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 4:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Avanthea Williams: age 20. Her body was found in an abandoned, boarded up apartment building scheduled for demolition at 10th and Minnesota by a demolition crew. Her body was thought to have been in the building for at least two months. The body was boarded up in the building, and the last time authorities were aware of the boards being removed had been in June.  She was wearing white pants, a volleyball t-shirt, and a gold necklace          when she was found on the floor in an empty room.&#34; <BR> <BR>From: <a href="http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/wicoca.html" target=_top>http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/wicoc a.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2295-->
<!--Post: 2355--><!--Time: 1103569999-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I disagree that this is a BTK case for 1 reason. BTK wants his victims to be found in a timely manner. As proven if the aren&#39;t a telephone call follows as done previously. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2355-->
<!--Post: 5633--><!--Time: 1107227796-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5633"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 7:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Avanthea &#40;Thea as we knew her&#41; was a known prostitute in Wichita. BTK has said he will take a prostitute. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5633-->
<!--Post: 7819--><!--Time: 1108692189-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK only cares about the MO he had set long ago in the Otero letter.  Bind them, Torture them, Kill them. <BR> <BR>There are not many facts to this case that we know of, and I wish we had more.  If we knew what state of condition the body was in &#40;i.e. was it bound&#41; then that could raise some warning bells. <BR> <BR>Tbear:  Vick Wergele was not found in a timely matter at all, and took years before the BTK announced her death was by his hands.  Since Avanthea was discovered after Vicky&#39;s murder then it is possible that BTK had done a slight &#34;MO change&#34; and stopped announcing his deaths so soon. <BR> <BR>If this MO change did take place it was within the limits he had set in the Otero letter.  That is if Avanthea was tortured and bound.  <BR> <BR>IMO:  I think we need more information, but I don&#39;t find anything that directly makes me say &#34;not BTK&#34; <BR> <BR>Cawichitan:  When did BTK say he wanted to take a prostitute?  I know that in a letter he admitted to solicitating them ...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7819-->
<!--Post: 9487--><!--Time: 1109538550-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9487"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If her necklace was left on, then I don&#39;t see any connection to BTK.  That necklace would have been to &#34;eye-catching&#34; for him not to take.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9487-->
<!--Post: 10965--><!--Time: 1110321199-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10965"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 2:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think BTK is responsible for this murder.  I don&#39;t think his leaving the package in Murdock Park was just a coincidence; I think it was a clue.  Look at how close in proximity the cereal box was to the Park City murders.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10965-->
